  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146408",
      "title": "Using The \"next-auth\" Library",
      "lectureOrder": 397,
      "videoOrder": 365,
      "sourceHash": "848418cf0c27254f4b9f2c1dfed96a9ee7e091073d22783b6eac1fa1a2ca96ff",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.05,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "As I mentioned in the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 7.14,
          "en": "we don't need to build everything from scratch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.14,
          "end": 10.86,
          "en": "Instead there is a package, the NextAuth package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.86,
          "end": 14.68,
          "en": "which we can use for implementing authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.68,
          "end": 18.13,
          "en": "Now the NextAuth package makes adding authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.13,
          "end": 21.54,
          "en": "to your next application super, super simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.54,
          "end": 24.29,
          "en": "And it actually supports a broad variety",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.29,
          "end": 27.31,
          "en": "of authentication for writers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.31,
          "end": 30.39,
          "en": "So you can't just go with your own email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.39,
          "end": 32.12,
          "en": "and password combination.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.12,
          "end": 36.32,
          "en": "You can also easily add Sign In with Google or Facebook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.32,
          "end": 39.273,
          "en": "or Apple or whatever you want with NextAuth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.65,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "The documentation of course is the place to go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 46.6,
          "en": "And there, if you click on authentication providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.6,
          "end": 49.18,
          "en": "you'll see a list of supported providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.18,
          "end": 50.81,
          "en": "and if you click on one, you'll learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.81,
          "end": 54.75,
          "en": "how to implement authentication with that provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.75,
          "end": 58.05,
          "en": "So that is something you absolutely can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.05,
          "end": 60.1,
          "en": "Now here in this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.1,
          "end": 63.03,
          "en": "we will not use one of those providers though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.03,
          "end": 65.61,
          "en": "but instead we will build it from scratch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.61,
          "end": 68.47,
          "en": "with our own email password combination",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.47,
          "end": 72.16,
          "en": "stored in our own database so that we can really see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.16,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "the complete authentication flow in greatest detail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.45,
          "end": 80.4,
          "en": "Now therefore that is the package we are going to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.4,
          "end": 82.33,
          "en": "and hence to get started,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.33,
          "end": 86.32,
          "en": "what we'll do is we'll first of all install NextAuth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.32,
          "end": 87.283,
          "en": "So in our project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.283,
          "end": 92.00999999999999,
          "en": "or quits to dev server and NPM, install NextAuth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.00999999999999,
          "end": 96.37,
          "en": "To install this NextAuth package next to dash-auth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.37,
          "end": 99.6,
          "en": "We'll install that and the NextAuth package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.6,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "has both server-side and client-side capabilities.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 107.53999999999999,
          "en": "We'll be able to use it on some API routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.53999999999999,
          "end": 110.97,
          "en": "to verify if a user is logged in and we'll be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.97,
          "end": 113.78999999999999,
          "en": "to use it in our components to do the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 116.34,
          "en": "Because of course the answer to the question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.34,
          "end": 118.1,
          "en": "whether a user is logged in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.1,
          "end": 122.96,
          "en": "and authenticated is not just needed on protected resources",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.96,
          "end": 126.17,
          "en": "on the server-side, so in our API routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.17,
          "end": 128.83,
          "en": "but also in our client-side components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.83,
          "end": 133.45,
          "en": "There we also might want to show a different user interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.45,
          "end": 137.18,
          "en": "based on whether a user is authenticated or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.18,
          "end": 140.27,
          "en": "And NextAuth will allow us to do both",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.27,
          "end": 143.59,
          "en": "server-side and client-side validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.59,
          "end": 147.32,
          "en": "It will also help us with generating those Auth Tokens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.32,
          "end": 149.82,
          "en": "Those JSON Web Tokens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.82,
          "end": 151.95,
          "en": "One thing it will not do though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 155.52,
          "en": "is manage user creation for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.52,
          "end": 158.82,
          "en": "We need to bring our own logic for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.82,
          "end": 161.7,
          "en": "It does support various databases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.7,
          "end": 165.07999999999998,
          "en": "but mostly for other authentication methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.07999999999998,
          "end": 168.86,
          "en": "And when it comes to having our own user accounts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.86,
          "end": 169.69299999999998,
          "en": "then we need to bring our own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.69299999999998,
          "end": 174.605,
          "en": "signup API route and our own user verification logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.52,
          "end": 178.57,
          "en": "But that's exactly what we're going to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.57,
          "end": 180.26,
          "en": "over the next lectures now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.26,
          "end": 182.16,
          "en": "and what we're going to explore there.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
